  "explains": "An annotation is added to the class InvoiceController: @CrossOrigin. An annotation on the class applies to every handler of the class, so the change is the class itself (a line of its header, not of a member) and every route of the controller is reached: seven routes (list, get, total, price, create, remove and lines). The first line of each chain is the added annotation. The routes the client calls (list, get and total, through fetchInvoices, fetchInvoice and fetchTotal) reach the screens /invoices and /invoices/:invoiceId. InvoiceControllerTest uses the controller. StatusController, AuditController, ReportController and CustomerController are other classes: their routes are not reached.",
  "complete_for": [
    "changed_symbol",
    "unit_test",
    "route",
    "screen",
    "http_edge",
    "finding"
  ],
